ern half of the San Luis Valley, including\nAntonito, Del Norte, Monte Vista and Alamosa.\n\n* WHEN...Through late Tuesday night.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone location.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Runoff from heavy rain and melting snow over the San Juan\nMountains may cause flooding in the San Luis Valley, especially\nMonday and Tuesday as high flows move out of the mountains and\nthrough the Rio Grande and Conejos River.\n- The greatest risk of flooding will be along the Conejos River and\nthe Rio Grande, including Del Norte, Monte Vista and Alamosa.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood http://cotrip.org","ends":"2026-11-04T05:00:00-07:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Del Norte Vicinity/Northern San Luis Valley Below 8500 Ft; Alamosa  Vicinity/Central San Luis Valley Below 8500 Ft; Southern San Luis Valley","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.a6499198bfeb3e5888538271cdeb42f7320e5f04.002.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.a6499198bfeb3e5888538271cdeb42f7320e5f04.002.1"},{"event":"Winter Storm Warning","headline":"Winter Storm Warning issued November 2 at 3:38AM MST until November 2 at 11:00AM MST by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"* WHAT...Heavy snow. Additional snow accumulations up to 3 to 6\ninches. Winds gusting as high as 50 mph.\n\n* WHERE...Eastern San Juan Mountains Above 10000 Feet.\n\n* WHEN...Until 11 AM MST this morning.\n\n* IMPACTS...Travel could be very difficult, especially tonight and\nMonday morning over Wolf Creek Pass and Cumbres Pass. Strong winds\ncould produce areas of blowing and drifting snow.","ends":"2026-11-02T11:00:00-07:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Eastern San Juan Mountains Above 10000 Ft","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.73e00f04c0d38244888300879b18131d33016053.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.73e00f04c0d38244888300879b18131d33016053.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Warning","headline":"Flood Warning issued November 1 at 4:16PM MST until November 2 at 4:15PM MST by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding along the Conejos River and other streams caused by\nlocalized rainfall, in addition to excessive rainfall and snow melt\nfrom higher elevations upstream, is expected.\n\n* WHERE...Eastern Conejos County in south central Colorado...\n\n* WHEN...Until 415 PM MST Monday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Flooding of rivers, creeks, streams, and other low-lying\nand flood-prone locations is imminent or occurring. Numerous roads\nremain closed due to flooding. Streams continue to rise due to\nexcess runoff from earlier rainfall. Expect many areas of slow\nmoving or standing water.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 414 PM MST, Doppler radar and automated rain gauges indicated\nheavy rain. Flooding is already occurring in the warned area.\nBetween 0.3 and 0.5 inches of rain have fallen.\n- Additional rainfall amounts of 1 to 2 inches are possible in the\nwarned area.\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nManassa, Sanford, La Jara, Antonito, Romeo, Capulin, Conejos,\nBountiful and Ortiz.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-11-02T16:15:00-07:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Conejos, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.dc7dc32149559b6690b7b7764bf9f5250586db02.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.dc7dc32149559b6690b7b7764bf9f5250586db02.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Warning","headline":"Flood Warning issued November 1 at 4:11PM MST until November 2 at 4:15PM MST by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding of area rivers and streams caused by rain and\nsnowmelt is expected.\n\n* WHERE...Western Conejos County in south central Colorado...\n\n* WHEN...Until 415 PM MST Monday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Flooding of rivers, creeks, streams, and other low-lying\nand flood-prone locations is imminent or occurring.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 410 PM MST, Rain and snowmelt is causing flooding. Between 1\nand 2 inches of rain have fallen.\n- Additional rainfall amounts of 2 to 3 inches are possible in the\nwarned area.\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nPlatoro, Cumbres Pass, and areas along Highway 17.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-11-02T16:15:00-07:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Conejos, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.6bdcad09d7929c655ae25a4a0c0235afc0975ee9.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.6bdcad09d7929c655ae25a4a0c0235afc0975ee9.001.1"},{"event":"Avalanche Advisory","headline":"Avalanche Advisory issued October 31 at 7:16PM MDT by NWS Denver CO","description":"SABCO\n\nTHE FOLLOWING MESSAGE IS TRANSMITTED AT THE REQUEST OF THE\nCOLORADO AVALANCHE INFORMATION CENTER.\n\n...A SPECIAL AVALANCHE ADVISORY IN EFFECT FROM 4:30 PM SATURDAY\nUNTIL 4:30 PM MONDAY...\n\n*WHAT...Avalanche conditions are dangerous above treeline.\n*WHERE...West Elk Mountains, Elk Mountains, San Juan Mountains, and\nLa Plata Mountains\n*WHEN...From 4:30 PM Saturday until 4:30 PM Monday.\n*IMPACTS...Backcountry travelers can easily trigger dangerous\navalanches large enough to bury a human.\n\n*PRECAUTION/PREPAREDNESS ACTIONS...A potent winter storm increases\navalanche danger Sunday into Monday. Rain, snow, and wind will cause\nnatural avalanches above treeline. Check the forecast at\nwww.colorado.gov/avalanche.\n\nBeyer & Pritchett","ends":"2026-11-02T16:30:00-07:00","severity":"Unknown","areaDesc":"West Elk and Sawatch Mountains; Northwestern San Juan Mountains; Southwest San Juan Mountains; Eastern San Juan Mountains Above 10000 Ft","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.5d9a0ec4f46df7deb3c2c0e5015df58147db243f.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.5d9a0ec4f46df7deb3c2c0e5015df58147db243f.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-11-02T11:25:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KPUB 021125 AFDPUB Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Pueblo CO 425 AM MST Mon Nov 2 2026 .KEY MESSAGES..